  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Normally, AFK detection procs when you enter the SteamVR overlay to use a browser or change settings and such. \n\nWhen using the Beyond, it does not do so, but at the same time, it will instead activate when your headset stays still for about 10 seconds, even if you're still wearing it. And not completely still: there does seem to be a threshold, probably to account for tracking error. \n\nThis might be an issue with the Beyond's drivers, but I'm inclined to say it isn't, since their AFK detection for dimming the screens is based on the proximity sensor. Perhaps it's leftover from development, if they were using the IMU to determine that the headset wasn't being actively used. \n\nAnyway, it's not a big issue, but I thought I'd report it anyway since it does affect some custom AFK animations that I made to let people know that the player is currently on their desktop or whatever.",
